  "body": "What happens: the post-merge batch gate is red on main. Two tests fail in the ui suite:\n\n- `detect_holes_note_tests::detect_holes_on_a_bore_op_with_only_a_wide_hole_is_refused`\n- `detect_holes_note_tests::detect_holes_on_a_bore_op_stores_the_small_hole_and_names_the_wide_one`\n\nExpected: the batch gate on the tip of main is green. A refusal-law test that fails means the bore hole-detection behaviour or its note changed without the tests.\n\nEvidence: run 43718974511 on head 8719d8b7a, job \"Batch gate tier\", step \"ui suites (cwd crates/ui)\". Each test failed in 78 s. The wall of the run was 37.5 min. Main moved 8719d8b7a through the bulk merge batch of 2026-11-15 (10 PRs). The report job was skipped, so this issue was filed by hand (the known bug in #1611).\n\nFindings: not bisected yet. The failing module is crates/ui/src/detect_holes_note_tests.rs. Start from the merges of the batch that touch hole detection or bore parameters.\n\nDone means: both tests pass in the batch gate on the tip of main, and the next green post-merge run closes this issue.\n",
